IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `coa-core`
IMPORT `coa26-support`
IMPORT `coa26-ch2b`
IMPORT `coa26-ch2a`

-- Tests for coa26-ch2a.l4 (ss 1212-1216). Expected values are written by hand from the text.

-- s 1212(1). order: subject to the body's rules, Schedule 10 recognition (MAYBE), eligible under the body's rules
#ASSERT `s 1212(1) the individual or firm is eligible for appointment as a statutory auditor` TRUE (JUST TRUE) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1212(1) the individual or firm is eligible for appointment as a statutory auditor` TRUE (JUST TRUE) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1212(1) the individual or firm is eligible for appointment as a statutory auditor` FALSE (JUST TRUE) TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1212(1) the individual or firm is eligible for appointment as a statutory auditor` TRUE (JUST FALSE) TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1212(1) the individual or firm is eligible for appointment as a statutory auditor` TRUE NOTHING TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 1212(1) the individual or firm is eligible for appointment as a statutory auditor` TRUE NOTHING FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 1212(2)
#ASSERT `s 1212(2) the person's eligibility for appointment as a statutory auditor is restricted as mentioned in section 1222` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1212(2) the person's eligibility for appointment as a statutory auditor is restricted as mentioned in section 1222` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 1213(1)
#ASSERT `s 1213(1) the person may act as statutory auditor of an audited person` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1213(1) the person may act as statutory auditor of an audited person` (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 1213(1) the person may act as statutory auditor of an audited person` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 1213(2) as a decision function. order: is a statutory auditor, becomes ineligible during the term of office
#ASSERT `s 1213(2) the statutory auditor must immediately resign and give notice` TRUE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1213(2) the statutory auditor must immediately resign and give notice` TRUE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1213(2) the statutory auditor must immediately resign and give notice` TRUE NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 1213(2) the statutory auditor must immediately resign and give notice` FALSE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 1213(3): (a) acts in contravention of (1), or (b) fails to give the notice
#ASSERT `s 1213(3) the person is guilty of an offence` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1213(3) the person is guilty of an offence` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1213(3) the person is guilty of an offence` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1213(3) the person is guilty of an offence` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 1213(4): on indictment a fine; on summary conviction a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum; no imprisonment
#ASSERT (`s 1213(4) the penalty for an offence under subsection (3)` `on conviction on indictment`)'s `fine not exceeding` EQUALS JUST `a fine without a stated limit`
#ASSERT (`s 1213(4) the penalty for an offence under subsection (3)` `on summary conviction`)'s `fine not exceeding` EQUALS JUST (`a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` 1)
#ASSERT (`s 1213(4) the penalty for an offence under subsection (3)` `on summary conviction in Scotland`)'s `fine not exceeding` EQUALS JUST (`a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` 1)
#ASSERT (`s 1213(4) the penalty for an offence under subsection (3)` `on summary conviction in England and Wales`)'s `fine not exceeding` EQUALS JUST (`a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` 1)
#ASSERT (`s 1213(4) the penalty for an offence under subsection (3)` `on summary conviction in Northern Ireland`)'s `fine not exceeding` EQUALS JUST (`a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` 1)
#ASSERT (`s 1213(4) the penalty for an offence under subsection (3)` `on conviction on indictment`)'s `imprisonment not exceeding` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`s 1213(4) the penalty for an offence under subsection (3)` `on summary conviction`)'s `imprisonment not exceeding` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`s 1213(4) the penalty for an offence under subsection (3)` `on summary conviction`)'s `how convicted` EQUALS `on summary conviction`
-- s 1213(4) in pounds: no figure on indictment; the statutory maximum (an input) on summary conviction
#ASSERT `s 1213(4) the most the person can be fined, in pounds` `on conviction on indictment` 5000 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 1213(4) the most the person can be fined, in pounds` `on summary conviction` 5000 EQUALS JUST 5000
#ASSERT `s 1213(4) the most the person can be fined, in pounds` `on summary conviction in Scotland` 10000 EQUALS JUST 10000
#ASSERT `s 1213(4) the most the person can be fined, in pounds` `on summary conviction in England and Wales` 5000 EQUALS JUST 5000
#ASSERT `s 1213(4) the most the person can be fined, in pounds` `on summary conviction in Northern Ireland` 5000 EQUALS JUST 5000
-- s 1213(5), (6)
#ASSERT `s 1213(5) the person is guilty of an offence` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1213(5) the person is guilty of an offence` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1213(5) the person is guilty of an offence` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1213(6) the person is guilty of an offence` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1213(6) the person is guilty of an offence` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1213(6) the person is guilty of an offence` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 1213(7): one-tenth of the greater of £5,000 and the level 4 amount, for each day; no limit on indictment
#ASSERT `s 1213(7) the penalty for an offence under subsection (5) or (6)` `on conviction on indictment` 2500 EQUALS `s 1213(7) a fine without a stated limit`
#ASSERT `s 1213(7) the penalty for an offence under subsection (5) or (6)` `on summary conviction` 2500 EQUALS `s 1213(7) a fine not exceeding a sum for each day on which the act or the failure continues` 500
#ASSERT `s 1213(7) the penalty for an offence under subsection (5) or (6)` `on summary conviction` 5000 EQUALS `s 1213(7) a fine not exceeding a sum for each day on which the act or the failure continues` 500
#ASSERT `s 1213(7) the penalty for an offence under subsection (5) or (6)` `on summary conviction` 8000 EQUALS `s 1213(7) a fine not exceeding a sum for each day on which the act or the failure continues` 800
#ASSERT `s 1213(7) the penalty for an offence under subsection (5) or (6)` `on summary conviction in Scotland` 8000 EQUALS `s 1213(7) a fine not exceeding a sum for each day on which the act or the failure continues` 800
#ASSERT `s 1213(7) the penalty for an offence under subsection (5) or (6)` `on summary conviction in England and Wales` 2500 EQUALS `s 1213(7) a fine not exceeding a sum for each day on which the act or the failure continues` 500
#ASSERT `s 1213(7) the penalty for an offence under subsection (5) or (6)` `on summary conviction in Northern Ireland` 2500 EQUALS `s 1213(7) a fine not exceeding a sum for each day on which the act or the failure continues` 500
-- s 1213(8): the defence needs both "did not know" and "had no reason to believe"
#ASSERT `s 1213(8) the defence is made out` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1213(8) the defence is made out` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1213(8) the defence is made out` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- s 1214(5)
#ASSERT `s 1214(5) the position counts as that of an officer or employee of the audited person for the purposes of subsections (2) and (3)` TRUE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1214(5) the position counts as that of an officer or employee of the audited person for the purposes of subsections (2) and (3)` FALSE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1214(5) the position counts as that of an officer or employee of the audited person for the purposes of subsections (2) and (3)` FALSE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1214(5) the position counts as that of an officer or employee of the audited person for the purposes of subsections (2) and (3)` FALSE NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 1214(2). order: counts as officer or employee (MAYBE), partner or employee of such a person, partnership of which such a person is a partner
#ASSERT `s 1214(2) this subsection applies to the person` (JUST TRUE) FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1214(2) this subsection applies to the person` (JUST FALSE) TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1214(2) this subsection applies to the person` (JUST FALSE) FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1214(2) this subsection applies to the person` (JUST FALSE) FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1214(2) this subsection applies to the person` NOTHING FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 1214(2) this subsection applies to the person` NOTHING TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 1214(3)
#ASSERT `s 1214(3) this subsection applies to the person` (JUST TRUE) FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1214(3) this subsection applies to the person` (JUST FALSE) TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1214(3) this subsection applies to the person` (JUST FALSE) FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1214(3) this subsection applies to the person` (JUST FALSE) FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1214(3) this subsection applies to the person` NOTHING FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 1214(4). order: a connection exists, it is of a description specified by regulations
#ASSERT `s 1214(4) this subsection applies to the person` TRUE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1214(4) this subsection applies to the person` TRUE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1214(4) this subsection applies to the person` TRUE NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 1214(4) this subsection applies to the person` FALSE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 1214(6)
#ASSERT `s 1214(6) the undertaking is an associated undertaking of the audited person` (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1214(6) the undertaking is an associated undertaking of the audited person` (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1214(6) the undertaking is an associated undertaking of the audited person` (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1214(6) the undertaking is an associated undertaking of the audited person` (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1214(6) the undertaking is an associated undertaking of the audited person` (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 1214(6) the undertaking is an associated undertaking of the audited person` NOTHING (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 1214(1): may not act if one or more of (2), (3), (4) apply
#ASSERT `s 1214(1) the person may act as statutory auditor of the audited person` (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1214(1) the person may act as statutory auditor of the audited person` (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1214(1) the person may act as statutory auditor of the audited person` (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1214(1) the person may act as statutory auditor of the audited person` (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 1214(1) the person may act as statutory auditor of the audited person` NOTHING NOTHING (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1214(1) the person may act as statutory auditor of the audited person` NOTHING NOTHING (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING

